title ALES210 — Lotus's mid/side: the stereo master read as its sum and its difference, the reversible primitive the width family spends
prompt Recur the road Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, send each finished increment, stop at custody gates, baton prin recur
think Read REMEMBER (living-edge card), the 1,024-round itinerary, and the six-season double-seat; the true git edge is Season C Lotus (ALES ladder), latest ALES209 stereo_reverb_freeze, the freeze axis closed whole for mono and stereo
think ALES209's design read and log both name width next, noting width wants its OWN mid/side primitive and so opens a small primitive round before the reverb rung that spends it — so the crux-first next lap is the primitive, not another one-off effect
think Lindy-first choice: a reusable reversible primitive (spent by width, mono-compatibility checks, side-only EQ) outlasts a one-off effect; built lotus/mid_side.rye — encode folds L/R into mid=(l+r)/2 and side=(l-r)/2, decode folds back l=saturate(mid+side), r=saturate(mid-side)
think Honest rail: encode never clips (proven in place, still routed through ALES2's one saturate so the rail lives in one place); the side is HALVED to stay on i16, so one bit cannot be stored — decode(encode) is EXACT where l+r is even and off by at most one LSB otherwise, named not hidden. A centred master (l==r) encodes to all-zero side and always round-trips exact (mono-compatibility)
think Both ops total (void, no EditError), balance asserted on entry/exit, exactly as ALES127 stereo_invert; five laws proven byte-for-byte in the selftest; caught one hand-computed test value before the run — divTrunc(-1,2)=0 not -1 for the (32767,-32768) mid — fixed, then GREEN on the metal pass
obs Discovery worth recording: the lotus/README.md front door has drifted well behind the code — its Status line stops at ALES159 and the Prove-the-rungs block at ALES29, and none of ALES160–209 touched it; REMEMBER's living-edge line still names DREY and its git nib was stale too. Per docs-sync (a ratchet, not a sweep) I shipped the rung without churning the stale front door, and flag a dedicated Lotus README + REMEMBER living-edge sync round as its own future lap
obs Kept the mono-then-stereo rhythm's spirit: this primitive is channel-symmetric (no mono/stereo split); the width rung it opens (mono then stereo, scale the side and recombine, spending ALES8's proven fader) is next
